            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0545" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.841 Surtax/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-11T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1927—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 11—12:48
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>718. Department’s 280, July 9, 2 p.m.; Legation’s 708, July 9, noon;<anchor
                        n="90" xml:id="d511-f1"/> and second paragraph Legation’s 711, July 9, 4
                    p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Pursuant to the policy as set forth in telegram first mentioned, regarding
                        protest against recent illegal exactions imposed or to be imposed by
                        Nationalist regime, I reserved our Government’s position at the diplomatic
                        body meeting this morning.</item>
                    <label>[2.]</label>
                    <item>The following identic telegram is being sent to their respective consuls
                        at Shanghai by the other diplomatic representatives concerned: <quote
                            rend="blockquote">
                            <p>“American Minister having referred to his Government is not yet in a
                                position to join protest against increase of tonnage dues. You
                                should [keep?] in touch with American consul general [and] with all
                                other colleagues and protest individually without delay unless
                                consular body considers that situations warrants [<hi
                                    rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] delay of a few days when America
                                may be in a position to join.”</p>
                        </quote></item>
                </list>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
